  "worked_solution": "We need to isolate $y,$ so we will treat the other variables $w,x,$ and $z$ as constants. We can use the addition and multiplication principles to solve for $y.$\n\nFirst, we subtract $2xz$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2xz-3y & =4w \\\\ 2xz-3y-2xz & =4w-2xz \\\\ -3y & =4w-2xz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $-3$ to get $y$ alone:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3y & =4w-2xz \\\\ \\frac{-3y}{-3} & =\\frac{4w-2xz}{-3} \\\\ y & =\\frac{4w-2xz}{-3} \\\\ y & =\\frac{2xz-4w}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
